+
+### Quick Mood toggle in the header, nav-shimmer diagnosis, rune-texture mockup (patch 0336)
+
+```discord-update
+Dev Update | Quick Mood Toggle
+- Added a quick day/night toggle next to the mute button -- flips Settings -> Guild's Mood without leaving your current tab
+```
+
+Direct request: "next to the mute button there should be a quick toggle
+(like settings already has the option for) to change the current mood
+night/bright (moody/bright)." Same header-button shape the mute control
+already established (MenuWindow.tsx) -- icon reflects the current
+RESOLVED mood (via `resolveBackgroundMood`, the same helper `backgroundSrc`
+itself already uses to pick art), not the raw setting, so it reads
+correctly even while on System. Clicking sets an explicit `dim`/`bright`
+value, the opposite of whatever's currently showing -- deliberately
+leaves System mode when clicked, the same way manually picking Moody or
+Bright in Settings would. 🕯️ shown while Moody, ☀️ while Bright, same
+icon choices GuildNamingModal's own Mood step already uses.
+
+**Nav-tab shimmer ("Guide, Enchanter, Notification icon aren't moving"),
+investigated with the actual screen recording provided.** Pixel-tracked
+the brightest point of the gold ring across every frame of the clip --
+it sits at the exact same coordinate for the full 5.4 seconds, confirming
+this is genuinely frozen, not just slow (an earlier static-analysis pass
+last patch couldn't tell the difference without seeing it live). Traced
+to the most likely real cause: `:root[data-motion='off']` (app.css)
+collapses EVERY animation in the app to a 1-frame freeze the moment
+`Settings -> Reduce Motion` is on -- and that setting defaults to ON
+for any new save created in an environment reporting the OS-level
+`prefers-reduced-motion` preference (`prefersReducedMotionByDefault`,
+settings.ts), which is common in VM/remote-desktop/test environments
+like the one the recording was likely captured in. This exact failure
+mode already has a documented precedent in this same file's own history
+(a prior bug description literally calls this shape out as "the real
+explanation" for a previous long-standing "animations play instantly"
+report) -- strong enough of a match that this needed confirming before
+writing any CSS, not another guess. Not fixed yet -- asked to check
+Settings -> Reduce Motion first, since if it's on, a frozen shimmer may
+be entirely correct, intended accessibility behavior rather than a bug
+at all.
+
+**Rune texture in the nav sidebar -- mocked up, not implemented,** per
+direct request ("mock it up first so i can see the design"). Generic
+Visualizer mockup styling (flat/light claude.ai chrome) wouldn't
+accurately represent this game's actual dark UI, so this used real color
+values pulled straight from app.css (--panel, --brass, --edge, etc.)
+in a standalone HTML file instead -- a faithful sidebar recreation, not
+an approximation. Five side-by-side options: baseline (no texture), the
+uploaded runes.png tiled at 130px in a brass tint at 4% and 8% opacity,
+the original dark-navy coloring inverted/brightened at 10%, and an 8%
+brass version applied to both the sidebar AND the titlebar for
+comparison. Delivered as a file for direct visual review -- no source
+changes made pending a pick.
